  questionText: Why is the diagonal line used in the paper scale?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: To get the least count of the paper scale the diagonal line is
    drawn. The diagonal line divides one centimetre length into smaller divisions.
  options:
  - To get the least count of the paper scale
  - Just like that
  - To measure the area of an object
  - To measure the volume of an object
